// Surveyor Hale, godwit, the Meridian Guild (6.9, optional). The ninth stone at dusk (Stones_3). He is finishing
// a secret survey of the Steppe; nine stones and the Guild can anchor Windreach. The ninth is the uncarved one:
// wherever the clan is standing (River_Idrenne_Night). He cannot sight it until somebody stands there.
// Voice: professional, courteous, a colleague to her. Works alone; does not say "we".

title: Stones_Hale
---
<<if has_flag("boss.hale.defeated")>>
    <<jump Stones_Hale_Pages>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("windreach.hale.decided")>>
    <<if has_flag("windreach.hale.finished")>>
        Hale: Nine of nine. Filed. I'll take the long road home. Lovely grass. #still #line:0c5701b
    <<else>>
        Hale: The ninth won't sit for the lens. Professional courtesy: I'm waiting for you. #still #line:001ab5c
    <<endif>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Hale: Journeyman. Professional courtesy: I'll finish first. #line:0e4b541
Hale: Eight stones sighted. The ninth, and the Guild can anchor the Steppe. The Guildmaster asked for it himself. #line:084b2cf
-> Not this one. Put the lens down. #line:06b6877
    Hale: Then it's a duel. The only kind two surveyors can have. Mind the stones. #line:0006b2b
    <<voice warden windreach>>
-> Why won't the ninth sit for you? #line:0576cd1
    Hale: It moves. I don't know how a stone moves. Four nights I've sighted it. #line:0facb28
    Hale: Help me, or stop me. I'd take either. #line:08a8460
    <<voice surveyor windreach>>
    -> Then I'll stop you. #line:0c06ac8
        Hale: Fair. Mind the stones. #line:018d382
        <<voice warden windreach>>
    -> Stand there. I'll hold the staff. #line:0e618fc
        <<voice drift windreach>>
        <<jump Stones_Hale_Finish>>
-> Finish it, then. #line:031763f
    <<voice drift windreach>>
    <<jump Stones_Hale_Finish>>
<<flag windreach.hale.challenged 1>>
<<flag windreach.hale.decided 1>>
===

title: Stones_Hale_Finish
---
Hale: Thank you. Truly. Hold it there. Somebody standing is all it wanted. #line:0034a90
Hale: Nine. The Steppe is on the Guild's map. They'll send a stone within the year. #line:039ba34
<<flag windreach.hale.finished 1>>
<<flag windreach.hale.decided 1>>
===

title: Stones_Hale_Pages
---
<<if has_flag("windreach.hale.pages")>>
    Hale: I'll tell them the grass ate it. It does, you know. #still #line:0596765
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Hale: Eleven months of pages. I can't tear them. You do it. #line:0572ce1
-> Burn them. All eleven months. #line:0afd9e9
    Hale: Yes. Better you than me. Keep the lens. I won't need it. #line:0fda26c
    <<flag windreach.hale.pages 1>>
    <<voice warden windreach>>
-> I'll keep them. Nobody else will. #line:0d018fe
    Hale: A survey only you hold. Isolde would have laughed. Keep the lens too. #line:0d00bf5
    <<flag windreach.hale.pages 2>>
    <<voice surveyor windreach>>
-> ... #line:06ba850
    Hale: Silence. Fair. I'll burn them on the road myself. Take the lens. #line:0c34540
    <<flag windreach.hale.pages 1>>
    <<voice drift windreach>>
<<flag windreach.hale.lens 1>>
<<flag windreach.hale.decided 1>>
===
